The `last-input` recording is not included. The node's `with` clause grants only Clock, HTTPClient and Notifier, and none of them gives access to a shared store. Writing `last-input` would mean importing `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, which is authority this node was not given, so the build would reject it. If you need that record, add a `StateHandle<'…', read-write>` to the node's `with` clause in the graph, and the body can then do the `put` without changing its output. The output is unchanged. If the notifier refuses the message on every try, the node traps rather than return a report that breaks `notified == true`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

const NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 3;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        // Clock: read the wall time once.
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // HTTPClient: one permitted fetch. A transport failure is a value and
        // counts as zero characters fetched; an out-of-allowlist URL traps at
        // the host boundary.
        let fetched: u32 = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => {
                let n = body.chars().count();
                if n > u32::MAX as usize {
                    u32::MAX
                } else {
                    n as u32
                }
            }
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        // Notifier: the contract requires `notified == true`. Retry a few
        // times; if the channel never accepts, trap rather than emit a
        // report that violates the ensures clause.
        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat at {}: fetched {} chars from {}",
            seconds, fetched, feed_url
        );
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS {
            if notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if !notified {
            panic!("notifier did not accept the heartbeat notification");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

